From: ac678@lafn.org (Donald Rose)
Date: Tue, 6 Dec 1994 15:59:36 -0800
Subject: [#94-12-241] can we change this Mailing List into a NEWSGROUP ?? and why

I love the messages sent around this list, the ideas, the people --
but I admit the daily flood of messages is exceeding my mail quota
constantly.  Also, there is the need to store messages on my home PC
(Mac, that is :-)  in order to access cool stuff from the past on
occasion.  

For these and other reasons, I propose we change from a List to a
USENET Newsgroup.  This way there is ONE place where each message is
sent, rather than hundreds (or how ever many folks are on the List today).
(This also cuts down on net overhead, having to send so many identical
messages to so many people on a List).

One argument against this might be that we want to keep these messages
"to ourselves" for some reason (I.e., "keep out riff raff")> Personally, I
don't think this is a major concern; besides, the flipside is that new people
who didnt know we exist can join in and read the great content we are sharing.

Please let me/others know what you think (reply to the List please; I'll
read the replies there!!). thanks --Donald

